(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphCausalGraph", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"35c95b33-4d19-8c43-9c99-fa8dcf4d32ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphCausalGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"sys", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"28233201-7a9c-9348-ba19-f05533a70219"],
 " ",
 "gives the causal graph of the rewriting system sys evolved n generations."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"5731eb02-360c-0346-90c1-97fe2e28ed6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphCausalGraph", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rules", ",", " ", "init", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]],
   "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"afae9b71-18fd-6548-9e45-04ad04d48f86"],
 " ",
 "builds the system first."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"92f9ec49-06bb-0d43-b5c1-ffad551847ad"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"52e0a2ed-9e92-954f-9818-b98c0138cbe6"],

Cell["\<\
The graph has one vertex per event, numbered as in sys[\"EventList\", n], and \
an edge from an event to a later one that depends on it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0519e309-3f99-8d43-8f43-29a40be7d2f7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two events are dependent when the elements they touch overlap. What counts \
as an element is the option \"CausalDependence\"; see ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["$CausalDependenceTypes", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"db2a0bde-8ce8-3341-8e33-7dd7b271b67c"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ca6e767b-7112-154c-b3c3-c41389cf67c5"],

Cell["\<\
An event touches what its match covered together with what it created. Along \
a path that comes to the same thing as the usual created-then-consumed \
reading, since an edge an event consumed is gone and can only be met again by \
having been created.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5252766e-6c0c-ec44-aa24-d4e5c30e98e5"],

Cell["\<\
Dependence is only asked about between events on one path: the second must \
act on the state the first produced, or on a descendant of it. In a multiway \
evolution two events on different branches never meet, whatever they have in \
common.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"468c09c0-0f9a-8e44-94a5-103a55794332"],

Cell["\<\
\"TransitiveReduction\" -> True, the default, leaves only the edges the order \
does not already imply.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8a83d488-ff10-3f43-a564-37077d137dc8"],

Cell["\<\
sys[\"CausalEdges\", n] gives the same relation as a list of associations \
with \"From\", \"To\", \"SharedEdges\" and \"SharedVertices\", which say not \
only that two events are related but what they had in common.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1746efc0-1899-d04b-b7d4-41a964845648"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"d1cb752c-392f-7b4a-baec-8b7cef3cd458"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing either edge of a two-edge path, and then either edge of the \
result:\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"bce80fda-a8cb-2542-be67-18d10fca2c58"],

Cell["\<\
subdivide = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}];
twoEdges = HypergraphRewritingSystem[subdivide, Hypergraph[{{1, 2}, {2, \
3}}]];
HypergraphCausalGraph[twoEdges, 2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f779d038-ceb4-3741-9185-9223d55f1112"],

